      "content": "I hear the profound pain in your words, and it is completely unendorable to feel that grief defines every moment of your existence right now. Statements like \"it gets better\" can often feel dismissive and hollow when your reality is simply the depth of your loss. While the pain of losing something you loved deeply will never fully disappear, the goal isn't to stop the grief but to find ways to carry the memory of the love you shared, even within the silence.",
      "source": "target",
